WEBVTT

00:02.410 --> 00:04.340
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

00:04.340 --> 00:06.270
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

00:06.270 --> 00:11.640
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

00:07.270 --> 00:13.240
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

00:11.640 --> 00:14.170
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

00:14.170 --> 00:15.840
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

00:30.360 --> 00:32.170
Leave this to me.

00:37.420 --> 00:40.180
Was Hevee's strength <i>that</i> superhuman?

00:40.180 --> 00:45.430
<i>I knew he had Blessing of Might, but I 
guess he's been holding back quite a bit.</i>

00:45.690 --> 00:49.190
Whatever happened to him 
being against telling lies?

00:54.840 --> 00:57.440
A-Are you some monster?

00:57.690 --> 01:00.080
Is a clergyman supposed to murder people?!

01:00.740 --> 01:04.200
I am a mere human before I'm a clergyman.

01:05.080 --> 01:06.330
I-I'm sorry!

01:06.810 --> 01:08.270
I'll stop being bad!

01:08.270 --> 01:10.710
S-So just spare my life!

01:10.710 --> 01:17.200
The gods say, death is serene,
and it comes to everyone impartially.

01:17.730 --> 01:20.480
But there is one point on 
which I beg to differ.

01:20.480 --> 01:21.530
W-Wait!

01:21.530 --> 01:22.720
I'll pay you any amount!

01:22.720 --> 01:26.730
Death must not be impartial 
when it comes to scumbags.

01:26.730 --> 01:29.040
And all the women you want, so—

01:41.870 --> 01:46.380
Don't think you can make such a 
fool of me and get away with it!

01:47.490 --> 01:50.200
You guys are finished.

01:55.050 --> 01:58.930
<b>Blizzard in the Desert</b>

01:57.260 --> 01:59.710
This must be the stratum lord!

01:59.710 --> 02:04.470
The ogre stratum lord said to dwell on 
the top floor of the Desert Pillar?

02:04.470 --> 02:06.850
You're all finished.

02:06.850 --> 02:09.510
Now wake up, Dual Ogre!

02:10.810 --> 02:11.990
Mealtime?

02:11.990 --> 02:13.110
Mealtime.

02:13.110 --> 02:15.610
Feel free to eat them, monster.

02:18.150 --> 02:20.310
Hey! Stop!

02:20.310 --> 02:21.580
I'm your—

02:24.620 --> 02:27.210
I will not yield my prey.

02:27.210 --> 02:28.590
Hey you!

02:28.590 --> 02:29.950
Don't steal from us!

02:29.950 --> 02:34.220
Right back at you. I staked 
my claim on him first.

02:35.830 --> 02:37.210
<i>F-ight t-igh-m.</i>

02:37.210 --> 02:38.330
Yeah!

02:42.180 --> 02:43.810
I'll deal with him!

02:43.810 --> 02:44.970
Be careful!

02:45.330 --> 02:47.510
I promised you I'd help!

02:47.510 --> 02:49.600
I appreciate it.

02:49.600 --> 02:52.730
Let's hurry up and take down this monster!

02:52.730 --> 02:55.990
With Master Boxxo and everyone here,
we won't have any problem!

02:58.650 --> 03:01.410
Meat! Meat! Can we eat?

03:01.410 --> 03:03.500
I want the thighs and entrails!

03:03.890 --> 03:07.240
<i>Time for this stratum's final showdown!</i>

03:15.250 --> 03:17.070
You underestimate humans too—

03:17.070 --> 03:18.620
No way! Run, everybo—

03:19.350 --> 03:21.640
<i>Uh-oh! Barrier time!</i>

03:22.630 --> 03:25.630
Points decreased by 2,222.

03:25.630 --> 03:26.940
<i>Huh?!</i>

03:26.940 --> 03:31.020
<i>When I only lost a </i>thousand<i> points when that 
monstrous Eight-Legged Crocodile rammed me?!</i>

03:32.560 --> 03:34.420
You won't smash us.

03:35.270 --> 03:37.770
Why didn't that take it down?!

03:39.360 --> 03:41.400
<i>Too bad. Too bad. Too bad.</i>

03:41.400 --> 03:44.900
<i>If those attacks keep hitting 
me, I'll be scrap in no time!</i>

03:44.900 --> 03:47.740
This is beyond us. Let us retreat!

03:53.020 --> 03:54.020
<i>Not a good plan!</i>

03:54.020 --> 03:57.160
<i>Come to think of it, this is the first 
time we've fought a stratum lord head-on!</i>

03:57.160 --> 03:59.220
<i>Until now, we've exploited their weak points!</i>

03:59.220 --> 04:03.670
<i>And being under the Netherlord's command 
might have made them weaker than usual!</i>

04:03.670 --> 04:05.930
<i>Form change!</i>

04:13.150 --> 04:13.890
This way!

04:13.890 --> 04:14.940
Let's split!

04:16.320 --> 04:19.350
Don't run away!

04:19.350 --> 04:21.520
<i>As if that would make anyone stop running!</i>

04:24.270 --> 04:27.280
Hey, Boxxo! There's a lot 
of loud noise behind us!

04:27.640 --> 04:29.780
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

04:42.130 --> 04:43.970
<i>Damn! What should I do?!</i>

04:43.970 --> 04:47.000
<i>Think! Water, ice, flames...</i>

04:49.520 --> 04:50.880
Lots of food!

04:50.880 --> 04:52.760
Meat! Meat!

04:52.760 --> 04:53.800
<i>Wha?</i>

04:55.940 --> 04:57.730
<i>I-It's eating monsters!</i>

04:57.730 --> 04:59.980
<i>Oh, I get it. They're really hungry.</i>

04:59.980 --> 05:02.210
<i>Their empty stomach must 
outweigh their anger!</i>

05:02.210 --> 05:03.260
<i>In that case!</i>

05:02.780 --> 05:03.320
<b>Umai Barbecue Sauce</b>

05:03.260 --> 05:07.460
<i>I'll give 'em my personal fave, 
authentic barbecue sauce!</i>

05:06.200 --> 05:07.950
<b>Umai Barbecue Sauce</b>

05:10.410 --> 05:11.450
What's that?

05:11.450 --> 05:13.190
It smells yummy!

05:14.990 --> 05:17.600
It <i>is</i> good!

05:19.960 --> 05:21.900
<i>That's the authentic stuff for you!</i>

05:21.900 --> 05:24.010
<i>This should buy us a little time!</i>

05:27.210 --> 05:32.510
Sorry. I should have told you more 
about the stratum lord in advance.

05:32.510 --> 05:35.480
What are we supposed to do 
against an opponent like that?

05:35.820 --> 05:40.670
<i>Normally, I'd respond with a carefree, 
"Hello there," but I don't know either.</i>

05:41.410 --> 05:44.090
I was a burden instead of being useful.

05:44.090 --> 05:46.180
I'm sorry, Master Boxxo.

05:46.180 --> 05:49.130
And I became angrier than I should have.

05:49.130 --> 05:52.240
I apologize for exposing everyone to danger.

05:52.630 --> 05:56.000
<i>T-igh-m to p-l-a-n.</i>

05:56.000 --> 06:00.010
He's right. Apologizing to one another 
will not improve the situation.

06:00.010 --> 06:02.620
Let us think on what to do about that ogre.

06:03.120 --> 06:04.930
We have two options.

06:04.930 --> 06:07.290
We run away from here, or we defeat it.

06:07.290 --> 06:09.430
It's too strong an opponent.

06:09.430 --> 06:11.300
I think we should consider running.

06:11.300 --> 06:13.880
Are you sure? We left Tashtay behind.

06:13.880 --> 06:18.760
Chances are, he's already dead, 
or the Dual Ogre will eat him.

06:18.760 --> 06:22.150
Even that skull ring didn't 
have it under control.

06:22.150 --> 06:25.440
The ring can only handle simple commands.

06:25.440 --> 06:27.210
When it comes to a stratum lord,

06:27.210 --> 06:29.860
signaling it to attack is probably 
the most one can hope for.

06:29.860 --> 06:31.910
Tashtay's skull ring.

06:31.910 --> 06:36.290
The Dual Ogre wouldn't take command 
if it ate that, would it?

06:36.960 --> 06:39.010
I'm sure that's...

06:39.010 --> 06:41.760
not necessarily impossible.

06:42.210 --> 06:46.550
In that case, the stratum lord would 
suddenly be in control of some monsters.

06:46.550 --> 06:49.390
If it were to go attack the village...

06:49.390 --> 06:53.130
I guess maybe we'd best 
take it down here and now.

06:53.130 --> 06:55.140
What do you think, Master Boxxo?

06:55.140 --> 06:59.390
<i>Would you mind not leaving a decision 
like that up to me, Mishuel?</i>

06:59.390 --> 07:04.670
<i>Um, guys, exactly what are you 
hoping for from a vending machine?</i>

07:04.670 --> 07:06.890
<i>But I guess I can't talk like that!</i>

07:06.890 --> 07:09.910
<i>O-er-s a-b-i-l-i-t-ease.</i>

07:10.170 --> 07:12.650
You want information first, huh?

07:13.700 --> 07:15.350
It has two heads.

07:15.350 --> 07:17.640
The right is male, the left, female.

07:17.640 --> 07:21.920
They seem to disagree on things sometimes, 
but they basically get along.

07:21.920 --> 07:25.790
Its body is harder than steel, 
and you've seen its power.

07:25.790 --> 07:29.430
It probably tops even Lammis, 
in terms of raw strength.

07:29.430 --> 07:31.610
My attacks are one thing,

07:31.610 --> 07:36.930
but can't attacks by Mishuel and Lammis 
penetrate something as strong as steel?

07:36.930 --> 07:39.540
Let's also discuss the Dual Ogre's blessings.

07:39.540 --> 07:41.940
I think you'll agree it 
has Blessing of Might?

07:43.720 --> 07:46.180
<i>Yeah, that power was off the charts.</i>

07:46.180 --> 07:48.530
And the problematic one is Hardening.

07:48.530 --> 07:50.190
That makes it way tougher all around.

07:50.190 --> 07:53.280
That would be why my attack didn't work.

07:53.280 --> 07:54.730
Blessing of Might and Hardening.

07:54.730 --> 07:57.570
It's simple, but that's what 
makes it so unmanageable.

07:57.570 --> 08:01.060
We maybe could have worked something 
out, if the captain were here.

08:01.060 --> 08:03.200
Yes, the Blessing of Eye-Breach.

08:03.200 --> 08:05.570
No use wishing for what we don't have.

08:05.570 --> 08:07.580
We'll have to work with what we've got.

08:07.580 --> 08:09.070
<i>True.</i>

08:09.070 --> 08:10.550
Also...

08:11.080 --> 08:13.350
I hear it's a big eater and a heavy drinker.

08:13.350 --> 08:16.170
<i>Huh, that sounds a lot like Japanese ogres.</i>

08:16.170 --> 08:19.390
<i>There are old tales about attacking 
them after you get them drunk.</i>

08:19.390 --> 08:21.260
<i>Drunk? Alcohol!</i>

08:21.260 --> 08:23.330
<i>I can offer it limitless alcohol!</i>

08:23.330 --> 08:24.450
<i>Okay!</i>

08:24.770 --> 08:27.360
<b>Ogre Killer</b>

08:27.520 --> 08:30.360
<b>Ogre Killer</b>

08:28.980 --> 08:30.360
<b>Bakufu Dance</b>

08:32.370 --> 08:33.840
This is...

08:34.650 --> 08:35.860
booze?

08:35.860 --> 08:37.590
There's so much of it.

08:37.590 --> 08:39.470
Do we get that thing to drink this?

08:39.470 --> 08:40.610
How?

08:40.610 --> 08:42.110
<i>Good point.</i>

08:42.110 --> 08:45.030
Maybe they'll drink if a 
pretty girl pours for them.

08:45.030 --> 08:47.920
We have no idea what an 
ogre would find beautiful.

08:48.210 --> 08:51.560
Hmm, what if it were a pretty ogre?

08:51.560 --> 08:52.920
Where would we find one?

08:52.920 --> 08:55.800
Can it be an ogre hallucination?

08:55.800 --> 09:00.580
I've had several encounters with ogres, 
so it's not out of the question.

09:00.580 --> 09:03.050
I don't know how to speak 
their language, though.

09:03.050 --> 09:06.230
I can teach you a smattering, at least.

09:06.230 --> 09:09.570
I don't know if it'll work or not,
but we might as well try.

09:09.570 --> 09:11.230
<i>Hello there.</i>

09:12.610 --> 09:16.070
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

09:15.020 --> 09:16.060
<i>Boxxo.</i>

09:16.350 --> 09:18.780
<i>A rock ogre monster.</i>

09:18.780 --> 09:21.320
<i>But it's actually Hevee,
with an illusion cast on him.</i>

09:21.760 --> 09:26.830
<i>And on his back is myself, transformed 
into a children's vending machine.</i>

09:26.830 --> 09:29.160
<i>Thirty 2L plastic bottles.</i>

09:29.160 --> 09:32.080
<i>All the water inside's been replaced 
with various alcoholic drinks.</i>

09:32.360 --> 09:34.210
Well, here goes.

09:35.460 --> 09:38.410
If you decide it's dangerous, 
come right back.

09:38.410 --> 09:40.230
Please be careful.

09:51.000 --> 09:52.090
Who're you?

09:52.090 --> 09:54.480
What's a rock ogre doing here?

09:55.490 --> 09:57.450
<i>That's ogre-speak we learned from Hulemy.</i>

09:57.450 --> 09:58.740
<i>It's an affirmation.</i>

09:59.490 --> 10:00.560
What's that?

10:00.560 --> 10:01.410
Water?

10:01.410 --> 10:03.530
<i>Now, get rid of the strings and caps!</i>

10:06.330 --> 10:07.440
This scent!

10:07.440 --> 10:08.860
It's booze?

10:11.620 --> 10:14.390
<i>It's true, they do like to drink!</i>

10:14.390 --> 10:16.620
<i>But it wouldn't hurt to slow down!</i>

10:18.330 --> 10:20.250
Gimme this one, too!

10:20.960 --> 10:22.160
That's good!

10:22.160 --> 10:24.140
I've never had a drink 
that tastes like this!

10:24.140 --> 10:26.020
More! More!

10:26.020 --> 10:28.160
I was just feeling thirsty, too!

10:28.160 --> 10:29.890
What a thoughtful rock ogre.

10:35.640 --> 10:37.310
<i>Is there enough?!</i>

10:37.310 --> 10:40.600
<i>But those two last bottles 
are the strongest!</i>

10:43.160 --> 10:46.310
I feel nice and sleepy.

10:46.310 --> 10:49.120
What a waste. Let's drink more.

10:59.440 --> 11:00.670
<i>It worked!</i>

11:01.070 --> 11:04.170
<i>Looks like a drunk ogre isn't 
going to wake up easily.</i>

11:06.660 --> 11:08.470
What do we do with that?

11:08.470 --> 11:10.440
It's filled with booze. Watch.

11:11.010 --> 11:12.950
Okay, the needle went in.

11:13.290 --> 11:16.810
Looks like they have to be 
conscious to use Hardening.

11:16.810 --> 11:19.940
This syringe was for injecting a 
chemical into the elder tree fiend,

11:19.940 --> 11:21.940
but it came in handy in an unexpected place.

11:23.950 --> 11:27.220
I feel bad for attacking 
it while it's asleep.

11:27.220 --> 11:31.540
It pains me as well, but I figure there's 
no need for pity in a duel to the death.

11:31.540 --> 11:33.200
Right, Master Boxxo?

11:33.200 --> 11:34.390
<i>Y-ea.</i>

11:34.390 --> 11:36.970
Well, I'll take this side.

11:36.970 --> 11:39.070
Can you deal with that side, Mishuel?

11:39.070 --> 11:39.990
All right.

11:39.990 --> 11:41.340
<i>L-a-i-s.</i>

11:41.340 --> 11:42.750
What is it, Boxxo?

11:42.750 --> 11:45.500
<i>B-ea-t th-e-m wi-th m-ea.</i>

11:45.500 --> 11:47.320
Huh? With you?

11:47.320 --> 11:48.260
<i>Y-ea.</i>

11:48.260 --> 11:52.800
I get it. If you defeat the enemy,
you'll gain points.

11:52.800 --> 11:54.270
<i>Y-ea, y-ea.</i>

11:54.270 --> 11:55.890
Oh, okay.

11:55.890 --> 11:59.030
Let's see, then. With Boxxo...

11:59.030 --> 12:01.700
Lammis, let's do this at the same time.

12:01.700 --> 12:02.780
Sure thing.

12:02.780 --> 12:04.410
One, two!

12:09.160 --> 12:11.040
<i>That's a stratum lord for you!</i>

12:11.040 --> 12:13.560
<i>Even though I split it three 
ways with Lammis and Mishuel,</i>

12:13.560 --> 12:15.790
<i>I got over a million points!</i>

12:15.790 --> 12:18.430
Is it all right if I absorb the Dual Ogre?

12:18.430 --> 12:19.960
Hang on a minute.

12:19.960 --> 12:23.700
There's a valuable part, and I'm cool 
with you doing it after I retrieve that.

12:24.210 --> 12:25.430
Go ahead, Kikoyu.

12:25.740 --> 12:27.350
Thank you.

12:40.940 --> 12:44.510
We'd better go check and see 
what became of Tashtay.

12:44.510 --> 12:47.190
Yes. Thank you.

12:50.690 --> 12:52.550
Isn't it kind of cold?

12:52.550 --> 12:54.920
Yeah. Is it coming from up above?

12:54.920 --> 12:56.470
This is strange.

12:56.470 --> 13:00.490
It's too much colder than the outside for 
it to be the night chill creeping in.

13:00.490 --> 13:02.930
What could this mean, Master Boxxo?

13:02.930 --> 13:04.900
<i>Don't ask me.</i>

13:11.800 --> 13:13.280
It's so cold!

13:13.280 --> 13:17.200
Very cold! Are we really 
in the middle of a desert?

13:17.460 --> 13:20.280
This cold... This sensation...

13:21.040 --> 13:22.060
Could it be?

13:27.580 --> 13:29.880
Huh? He's frozen in ice?!

13:29.880 --> 13:32.690
Everyone, please gather around Boxxo!

13:34.080 --> 13:35.830
Boxxo, your barrier.

13:35.830 --> 13:38.080
<i>Good call. Activate barrier!</i>

13:40.320 --> 13:43.020
Snow?! In the Scorching Sand stratum?!

13:43.020 --> 13:47.590
Whoa, I've never heard of any monster 
on this stratum that controls cold air.

13:58.370 --> 14:00.350
You are a snow fairy.

14:02.100 --> 14:05.290
You are mistaken if you 
regard us as enemies.

14:05.290 --> 14:08.850
We simply came here to see that man.

14:17.000 --> 14:18.880
Wh-What was that for?

14:18.880 --> 14:22.880
Snow fairies are not a race 
that wantonly kill people!

14:22.880 --> 14:26.010
What's a snow child doing with humans?

14:26.010 --> 14:27.930
These people are my friends!

14:27.930 --> 14:29.610
Humans are scum.

14:29.610 --> 14:31.500
You know that too, don't you?

14:31.970 --> 14:35.270
It's true that I've lived my 
life on the run from humans.

14:35.520 --> 14:40.850
<i>Director Bear told me before about the 
mysterious powers snow children like Kikoyu have.</i>

14:40.850 --> 14:44.050
It's said that if you behead a snow 
child on the day it becomes an adult,

14:44.050 --> 14:47.410
they turn into an ice 
statue that never melts.

14:47.410 --> 14:52.320
And that the severed head will 
continue to utter curses,

14:52.320 --> 14:54.530
resulting in regional contamination.

14:54.850 --> 14:57.670
But there are also humans you can trust!

14:57.670 --> 15:00.480
And not just humans,
but even dependable Field.

15:00.480 --> 15:02.670
There are many such people!

15:02.670 --> 15:06.570
You poor thing. The humans have tricked you.

15:06.570 --> 15:08.480
No they haven't! You misunderstand!

15:08.480 --> 15:10.420
We are not your enemies!

15:10.420 --> 15:11.680
Not my enemies?

15:11.680 --> 15:12.770
Indeed.

15:12.770 --> 15:15.470
Then you work for the Netherlord?

15:15.470 --> 15:17.930
The Netherlord?

15:21.180 --> 15:22.790
No, you must not.

15:22.790 --> 15:25.000
Now that I look closely at that steel box,

15:25.000 --> 15:28.810
it looks just like that Boxxo magic 
item of which the Netherlord spoke.

15:28.810 --> 15:31.830
<i>How about that? I'm famous 
and didn't even know it.</i>

15:31.830 --> 15:34.830
That means <i>you</i> work for the Netherlord?

15:34.830 --> 15:37.740
Yes, I am Medicine General Sulream.

15:37.740 --> 15:39.530
The Demon Lord's general?

15:39.530 --> 15:44.570
The Netherlord saved me just before some 
humans who caught me were about to kill me,

15:44.570 --> 15:46.840
and I've been by his side ever since.

15:47.110 --> 15:49.430
<i>That's so well timed it bugs me.</i>

15:49.430 --> 15:53.480
<i>What if the Netherlord set that up so he 
could get his hands on a snow fairy's powers?</i>

15:53.480 --> 15:55.350
<i>It's something he'd try.</i>

15:55.350 --> 15:58.500
His words mean everything to me.

15:58.500 --> 16:00.590
All of you stand in our way.

16:03.970 --> 16:05.790
<i>Points dropped by ten.</i>

16:04.900 --> 16:06.910
<i>Points dropped by ten.</i>

16:05.580 --> 16:07.720
<i>Points dropped by ten.</i>

16:06.600 --> 16:08.110
<i>Points dropped by ten.</i>

16:07.720 --> 16:09.080
<i>Points dropped by ten.</i>

16:08.200 --> 16:09.720
<i>Points dropped by ten.</i>

16:09.720 --> 16:13.240
We're in trouble. The second 
we step outside, we'll freeze.

16:13.240 --> 16:17.120
<i>Well, I have plenty of points, 
so I <i>could</i> tough this out.</i>

16:17.120 --> 16:20.990
Does every snow fairy have 
such incredible powers?

16:21.280 --> 16:25.300
We each differ, but it's unusual 
to see someone on this level.

16:25.300 --> 16:27.000
She is quite powerful.

16:27.000 --> 16:29.440
How long will this blizzard last?

16:29.440 --> 16:33.380
With her power, it might go 
on for two or three days.

16:33.630 --> 16:36.770
Boxxo, how long do you think 
your barrier will last?

16:36.770 --> 16:40.380
<i>Let's see, if I'm using 
up ten points a second.</i>

16:40.380 --> 16:42.010
<i>Based on my current points...</i>

16:42.310 --> 16:43.760
<i>W-u-n d-a-y.</i>

16:48.030 --> 16:50.310
<i>I'll try again to persuade her.</i>

16:50.310 --> 16:51.320
<i>How?</i>

16:51.320 --> 16:53.560
<i>I'll be fine even if I step outside.</i>

16:53.560 --> 16:54.690
<i>Really?</i>

16:54.690 --> 16:57.050
<i>Thank you for your concern.</i>

16:57.050 --> 17:00.000
<i>But I want to stop her.</i>

17:00.920 --> 17:04.690
<i>She is the me who never met Field.</i>

17:04.690 --> 17:10.140
<i>Had I also met the Netherlord before I met 
Field, I'm sure I'd turn out the same way.</i>

17:10.500 --> 17:12.140
<i>You feel sorry for her?</i>

17:12.490 --> 17:16.340
<i>I would be lying if I said I did not,
but there is more to it.</i>

17:16.340 --> 17:17.500
<i>Please trust me.</i>

17:17.800 --> 17:19.890
<i>Okay. I'll trust in that.</i>

17:19.890 --> 17:20.760
<i>But...</i>

17:20.760 --> 17:23.270
<i>Boxxo, what time is it?</i>

17:23.610 --> 17:27.380
<i>Um, it'll be midnight in less than a minute.</i>

17:27.380 --> 17:29.010
<i>Then I will be back!</i>

17:36.830 --> 17:39.920
<i>Say what? Those two are strangely calm.</i>

17:39.920 --> 17:41.280
<i>Do they know something?</i>

17:41.280 --> 17:44.580
Huh? Is snow also blowing 
from the opposite direction?

17:44.580 --> 17:47.550
And it's pushing back on 
the original blizzard?

18:03.800 --> 18:06.810
Um, who's that? A snow fairy?

18:06.810 --> 18:10.530
You think she's come to save us?

18:10.530 --> 18:14.450
Her boots are exactly the same as Kikoyu's.

18:14.450 --> 18:15.760
Master Boxxo.

18:15.760 --> 18:18.920
It's ballooned up far 
beyond what I felt before,

18:18.920 --> 18:21.400
but I sense the same type 
of energy as Kikoyu's.

18:21.400 --> 18:23.070
What could this mean?

18:23.070 --> 18:25.880
<i>That means, she's Kikoyu.</i>

18:25.880 --> 18:29.560
<i>I get it, she grew up 
in the blink of an eye.</i>

18:29.560 --> 18:31.090
<i>Wait, what?!</i>

18:31.090 --> 18:32.860
That's Kikoyu?

18:32.860 --> 18:34.470
Huh?! No way!

18:34.470 --> 18:38.210
I hear the moment snow fairies 
reach their eighteenth birthday,

18:38.210 --> 18:40.830
they suddenly grow into adults.

18:40.830 --> 18:43.840
Then today's Kikoyu's birthday?!

18:43.840 --> 18:48.530
<i>Oh! That's why she's been paying attention 
to her calendar the past several days!</i>

18:48.530 --> 18:50.390
<i>Today's the day with the 
red circle around it.</i>

18:50.390 --> 18:53.100
<i>And we just passed midnight!</i>

18:53.100 --> 18:56.070
Her magical powers are far 
beyond what they were.

18:56.070 --> 18:58.570
I didn't know the change 
would be so dramatic.

18:58.570 --> 19:01.820
She's rivaling the Demon Lord's 
general. That's so amazing!

19:01.820 --> 19:03.090
It's an equal match.

19:03.090 --> 19:05.480
No, Kikoyu is pushing back.

19:05.480 --> 19:08.730
This is my final request. 
Would you leave this place?

19:08.730 --> 19:11.160
I have something I need to do.

19:11.750 --> 19:13.770
I can't afford to die here.

19:13.770 --> 19:15.650
I have my own mission.

19:16.260 --> 19:18.250
Fine, I'll leave.

19:28.650 --> 19:32.280
It's still a little cold, 
but you can come out.

19:36.160 --> 19:38.900
Um, you are Kikoyu, right?

19:38.900 --> 19:40.960
Yes, that's right.

19:44.580 --> 19:47.830
I wish I could have seen the 
moment she became an adult.

19:47.830 --> 19:51.150
<i>I wonder if it's like a transformation 
sequence in a magical girl anime.</i>

19:51.150 --> 19:52.830
<i>I'd like to have recorded it.</i>

19:54.090 --> 19:57.590
Boxxo, are you having weird thoughts again?

19:57.590 --> 19:59.810
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

19:59.810 --> 20:02.080
There you go playing innocent again!

20:02.080 --> 20:06.660
Well, I guess we can say things 
are settled on this stratum, too.

20:06.660 --> 20:08.100
I feel bad for Hevee, though.

20:13.850 --> 20:15.650
Are you good to go?

20:15.650 --> 20:19.730
Yes. Tashtay received even more 
than he had coming to him.

20:19.730 --> 20:23.580
Besides, watching him suffer was 
probably never going to clear

20:23.580 --> 20:26.880
this haze that's inside my heart.

20:26.880 --> 20:27.870
And so...

20:28.550 --> 20:30.260
I am fine with this outcome.

20:30.610 --> 20:34.370
<i>Huh, I didn't know he could 
make such an uplifting face.</i>

20:34.680 --> 20:36.680
Looks like you're gonna be okay.

20:36.680 --> 20:40.480
Oh, were you concerned about me?

20:40.480 --> 20:43.650
Who'd be concerned about a boot pervert?!

20:43.650 --> 20:47.760
But then, I guess boots don't 
matter anymore. Too bad.

20:47.760 --> 20:51.640
If you were still feeling down, I would've 
been willing to give you my boots.

20:52.270 --> 20:54.890
Were you being sincere just now?

20:54.890 --> 20:58.520
Huh? You don't care about 
boots anymore, right?

20:58.520 --> 21:01.420
It's true that revenge was driving 
me to search for footwear,

21:01.420 --> 21:03.910
but it's also true that I've 
awakened to its appeal.

21:03.910 --> 21:07.390
Now, please make good on what you 
said and take off those boots.

21:07.390 --> 21:11.840
I have no interest in you personally, but I've
had my eye on your boots for some time.

21:11.840 --> 21:15.140
You're indifferent about your clothing,
so I suspect those boots you've been wearing

21:15.140 --> 21:17.040
will give off the most exquisite fragrance.

21:17.040 --> 21:18.670
Die, you freak!

21:18.670 --> 21:20.770
I take back what I said!

21:20.770 --> 21:22.680
I wanna play, too!

21:22.680 --> 21:24.290
That's too big!

21:24.290 --> 21:26.670
I can produce any amount of snow you like.

21:32.060 --> 21:35.130
<i>At some point, a snowball fight broke out.</i>

21:36.060 --> 21:39.070
Shall we take part as well, Master Boxxo?

21:39.070 --> 21:43.150
<i>Sure, a snowball fight on the Scorching 
Sand stratum sounds sweet.</i>

21:43.150 --> 21:44.600
<i>Hello there.</i>

23:19.780 --> 23:22.710
You know the ones the Netherlord is wary of?

23:22.710 --> 23:24.630
Boxxo and Lammis?

23:24.630 --> 23:29.300
Your group must assist 
me in dealing with them.

23:32.050 --> 23:34.150
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.680 --> 23:37.060
<i>You win!</i>

23:37.390 --> 23:45.140
<b>Season 3 is coming!</b>

23:37.390 --> 23:45.140
<b>Season 3 is coming!</b>
